# Superpowers Artifact Redirection

Whenever any Superpowers skill (brainstorming, writing-plans, executing-plans,
subagent-driven-development, requesting/receiving code review, etc.) would write
a design spec, implementation plan, task-status file, progress report,
code-review artifact, or other autogenerated artifact to its own default
location (`docs/superpowers/…` or similar), write it instead under this repo's
`.superpowers/` tree as follows.

## Committed design history (`.superpowers/docs/`)

- `.superpowers/docs/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md` — brainstorming design
  specs (plugin default was `docs/superpowers/specs/…`).
- `.superpowers/docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature-name>.md` — writing-plans output
  for single-plan features (plugin default was `docs/superpowers/plans/…`).
- `.superpowers/docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature>.phase.NN.md` — multi-phase
  plans use **dot-segmented** filenames (matching `002-monorepo-and-naming.mdc`).
- `.superpowers/docs/tasks/<feature-slug>.md` — lean living agent checklist.
  Status header fields: Current phase / Doing now / Model (doing now) / Next /
  Blocked on. Checklist items mirror each plan's `### Task N:` headings with
  `- [ ]` / `- [x]` and a short `model:` annotation (default Grok 4.6 per
  `012-agent-model-selection.mdc`; record escalations). Mutate in place after
  every completed task. Phase-plan step `- [ ]` boxes are static plan text —
  not execution state. No long prose here.
- `.superpowers/docs/progress/<feature-slug>.md` — append-only long narrative
  (decisions, blockers, detailed history). Point readers here from the tasks
  file; never dump that detail into `docs/tasks/`.

## Other committed buckets

- `.superpowers/reviews/<feature-slug>/` — requesting-code-review /
  receiving-code-review skill output for that feature.

## Plugin scratch (gitignored — do not commit)

- `.superpowers/brainstorm/` — visual companion sessions. The companion
  `start-server.sh` **hardcodes** this path; never rename to `brainstorming/`.
- `.superpowers/sdd/` — subagent-driven-development workspace (task briefs,
  implementer reports, review-package diffs, SDD progress ledger). The skill's
  `sdd-workspace` script creates it and writes a self-ignoring `.gitignore`.
  Never hand-create or commit files there.

Root `.gitignore` must list `.superpowers/brainstorm/` and `.superpowers/sdd/`.
Do **not** gitignore the rest of `.superpowers/` — design history is committed.
This is distinct from the personal `.devlog/` folder (git/cursorignored).

`<feature-slug>` is a kebab-case slug shared across `docs/tasks/`,
`docs/progress/`, and `reviews/` for the same piece of work (e.g.
`vicore-slate-scaffold`).

This rule loads before every other rule in this repository and must never be
deleted or disabled.
